<%# Card surface - the default container for a block of related content.

    Stripe/Airbnb reading: a card earns its edges from a hairline border and a
    low shadow, not a heavy drop shadow, with generous internal padding. Its
    header is separated by a hairline: the title and the data below it are two
    different things, and stating that boundary is what the references do.

    Locals:
      title    - optional heading text
      subtitle - optional supporting line under the title
      padded   - false to remove body padding (for flush tables)
      class    - extra classes on the outer element

    Body content is passed as a block, so render with `layout:`. %>
<% padded = local_assigns.fetch(:padded, true) %>
<section class="tw-card <%= local_assigns[:class] %>">
  <% if local_assigns[:title].present? %>
    <%# The header carries a rule, matching Stripe's Box, Primer's Box.Header and Tailwind
        UI's card-with-header. It was removed once on the strength of design.md's line about
        a border-b over-segmenting a card - but that line is about a *compact* content card,
        and it names the substitute structure it relies on ("that detail divider and the
        footer border-t"). Most cards here hold an attribute list or a table and have
        neither, so removing the rule left them with no boundary at all and the header
        floating 36px above its content. %>
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 px-5 py-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= title %></h2>
      <% if local_assigns[:subtitle].present? %>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600"><%= subtitle %></p>
      <% end %>
    </header>
  <% end %>

  <%# Padding either side of the header rule is symmetric, and smaller than the card's own
      p-5. With a full p-5 body under a py-4 header the seam carried 16px + 20px, measured at
      37px from the header text to the first line of content - which read as a gap rather than
      as a boundary. 16px either side (32px total) is what Stripe's Box and Primer's Box.Header
      use. A card with no header keeps the full p-5. %>
  <% body_padding = if !padded
                      ""
                    elsif local_assigns[:title].present?
                      "px-5 pb-5 pt-4"
                    else
                      "p-5"
                    end %>
  <div class="<%= body_padding %>">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</section>
